<div class="wrapper clearfix games-history">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <hr>
    <h3>Pig game rules:</h3>
    <hr>
    <p>The game has <b>2</b> players, playing in rounds. In each turn, a player rolls a dice as many times as he whishes.
        Each result get added to his <em>round</em> score. <em>But</em>, if the player rolls a '<b>1</b>' or '<b>6</b>'
        two times in a row,all his
        <em>round</em> score gets lost. After that, it's the next player's turn. The player can choose to '<b>Hold</b>',
        which meansthat his <em>round</em> score gets added to his <em>global</em> score. After that, it's the next
        player's turn. The first
        player to reach earlier set <em>winning score</em> on his <em>global</em> score wins the game.</p>
    <hr>
    <h3>Top Scores</h3>
    <hr>
    <p>Top scores are saved in local storage of user's browser, and contain name and score of player who won each game.
        If you want to clear the history of your games, just click '<b>Clear history</b>' button on <em>Top Scores</em>
        page.</p>
    <hr>
    <p><b>Node.js Pig Game, Copyright &copy; 2020 Szymon Hrehorowicz</b></p>
